t-alt:27px"><span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;"><stron=
g>What is in the new plan? </strong>Young people would no longer be able to=
 claim the two main sickness and disability benefits. Instead they would be=
 moved on to a new =E2=80=9Cyouth allowance=E2=80=9D, paid at the same leve=
l as the standard rate of universal credit.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=3D"ltr"=
=20
style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p><p dir=
=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;"><strong>What does =
this mean? </strong>Many of those who receive personal independence payment=
 (Pip) will move on to a new =E2=80=9Cadditional cost allowance=E2=80=9D, w=
hich will cover expenses relating to their conditions. Fewer people are lik=
ely to be entitled to it. Those with profound disabilities who are not capa=
ble of working would be given a new benefit, paid at a higher rate.&nbsp;</=
span></p><p dir=3D"ltr"=20
style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p><p dir=
=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px"><span s=
tyle=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;"><strong>What will happen =
instead? </strong>The review will recommend investing billions in employmen=
t support, including one-to-one personal advisers, work placements and job =
subsidies which would give young people a =E2=80=9Cmenu of options=E2=80=9D=
 to help them find work.&nbsp;</span></p><p dir=3D"ltr"=20
style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:21px">&nbsp;</p><p dir=
=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px"><span s=
tyle=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">Milburn will also call fo=
r immediate mental health support for those with mild attention deficit hyp=
